Subject: [PATCH 251/260] [ae-patch] Keep a transcript with a native image
 read, and log why a keep is refused

The transcript keep refused any file the clone sanitizer would change. Claude Code writes every native image read with a toolUseResult dict holding the image's base64, and the sanitizer collapses that to a short string without touching the message, so a session that had viewed an image since its last rebuild could never be kept. The check now refuses only for a change the model would see: the message differs after sanitizing, a string or list toolUseResult carries a payload, or an image result sits on a record whose message content is not a list. A record whose only change is the base64 in Claude's own image-read toolUseResult (type image, a file dict holding a string base64) stays as written. The kept file is not rewritten.

A refused keep now logs one INFO line naming the first check that failed: no cursor, no record, no server items, frontier does not hold (record count, server count and the known wire type of the first item past the record), record and cursor differ, path mismatch, not resumable, cursor fingerprint mismatch, tail incomplete, or sanitizer would change a message (with the line number). Ids, counts, types and line numbers only.
